# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Reproduces production before #4522's drain fix (#4566):
# the terminal
# drains a prepared bucket by skipping a key whose row is newer than the
# bucket and not migrated, and otherwise installs the saga's value at a fresh
# dominating stamp. A later write the split's shadow-forward imported onto the
# destination is a migrated row, so a bucket the sweep replayed there drains
# over it and the acknowledged write is lost. The intended design (#4566's
# Fix-M) drains a marked bucket last-writer-wins at its prepare stamp whatever
# the row's migrated flag says. The edit lies in TermRow, the operator the
# terminal broadcast applies, so the mutation declares no PERTURBS.
MODULE: NoKeyLostFreshStampDrainOverMigratedRow
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the drain skips only a newer non-migrated row and otherwise installs at a fresh stamp, overwriting a migrated later write

--- FIND
    ELSE IF pend[c][s][k] = "old" THEN LWW(row[c][s][k], BVal(c))
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: skip only a newer, non-migrated row; otherwise install at a fresh stamp.
    ELSE IF pend[c][s][k] = "old"
    THEN IF Stamp(row[c][s][k]) > Stamp(BVal(c)) /\ ~mig[c][s][k] THEN row[c][s][k] ELSE FreshV
--- END